**** Types of Const Pointers in C ****
1. Constant Pointer
2. Pointer to constant
3. Constant pointer to constant

**** Constant Pointer ****

- Address of the pointer can't be changed
- Value present in pointer can be changed

int x = 10, y = 20;
int *const ptr = &x;   // ptr always points to x
*ptr = 15;             // allowed: modify value at x
// ptr = &y;           // error: cannot change address

**** END ****

**** Pointer to constant ****

- Address of the pointer can be changed
- Value present in pointer can't be changed

int a = 5, b = 30;
const int *ptr = &a;   // ptr points to a
// *ptr = 10;          // error: cannot modify value
ptr = &b;              // allowed: change address

**** END ****

**** Constant pointer to constant ****

- Address of the pointer can't be changed
- Value present in pointer can't be changed

const int x = 50;
const int *const ptr = &x; // fixed address, fixed value
// *ptr = 60;              // error: cannot modify value
// ptr = &y;               // error: cannot change address

**** END ****
